---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---
<Base title="The Venue — Owen & Rowan" description="New Mexico Museum of Art, Santa Fe. Directions, what to expect, and how to find us.">
  <Breadcrumb />

  <article class="px-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto pb-24">

    <figure class="mb-16 -mx-6 md:mx-0" data-reveal>
      <img
        src="/illustrations/museum-facade.svg"
        alt="New Mexico Museum of Art"
        class="w-full"
        loading="eager"
        width="900"
        height="500"
      />
    </figure>

    <h1 class="type-display mb-4" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);" data-reveal>
      New Mexico Museum of Art
    </h1>
    <p class="type-label mb-16" style="color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-ink) 50%, transparent);" data-reveal>
      107 W Palace Ave, Santa Fe, NM 87501
    </p>

    <!-- About the space -->
    <section class="prose-wedding mb-16" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="type-label mb-6" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);">The Space</h2>
      <p>
        The New Mexico Museum of Art Plaza Building sits on the corner of Lincoln and Palace, one block from
        the Plaza, and has been one of Santa Fe's most important buildings since 1917. The
        architecture is Pueblo Revival (thick adobe walls, wooden vigas, portal columns), and is
        designed to look as if it had always been there. The ceremony will take place in the
        courtyard, which is one of the most beautiful enclosed outdoor spaces we know of.
        Full of flowers and with an open sky, the courtyard is surrounded by curved walls and a portal, with a fountain at the center.
      </p>
      <p>
        If there's an afternoon thunderstorm (July is monsoon season), the ceremony will move inside the museum. The building is beautiful either way,
        and New Mexico rain is brief and dramatic and exactly right for a wedding.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- What to expect -->
    <section class="prose-wedding mb-16" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="type-label mb-6" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);">What to Expect</h2>
      <p>
        Doors open at 5:00 pm and the ceremony will begin promptly at 5:30 pm. 
        A cocktail hour follows in the museum's interior spaces starting at 6:00 pm,
        then dinner and dancing from 7:00 pm until 11:00 pm.
      </p>
      <p>
        The evening ends at 11:00 pm. The Plaza and its bars and restaurants are a five-minute
        walk if the night has more in it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Getting there -->
    <section class="mb-16" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="type-label mb-8" style="color: var(--c-terracotta);">Getting There</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <div>
          <address class="not-italic leading-relaxed mb-6 prose-wedding">
            <strong class="type-label block mb-2">Address</strong>
            New Mexico Museum of Art<br />
            107 W Palace Ave<br />
            Santa Fe, NM 87501
          </address>
          <div class="flex gap-6">
            <a
              href="https://maps.apple.com/?q=107+W+Palace+Ave+Santa+Fe+NM"
              class="link-draw type-label"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Apple Maps ↗
            </a>
            <a
              href="https://maps.google.com/?q=107+W+Palace+Ave,+Santa+Fe,+NM+87501"
              class="link-draw type-label"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Google Maps ↗
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prose-wedding">
          <strong class="type-label block mb-4">Parking</strong>
          <p>
            The Museum does not provide official parking.
            We recommend <a
              href="/stay"
              class="link-draw"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >staying downtown
            </a> near the venue or taking an uber/lyft/taxi. There is also limited street parking nearby. The Santa Fe Place Mall parking structure on Sandoval St is a short walk and
            reliably has spaces.
            If driving please try to carpool.
          </p>
         
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Catering placeholder -->
    <section class="prose-wedding" data-reveal style="background: var(--c-base-warm); padding: 2rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--c-ochre);">
      <strong class="type-label block mb-3">Catering</strong>
      <p style="color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c-ink) 60%, transparent);">
        Caterer and menu details are being finalized. We'll update this page with full
        information — including dietary accommodation details — once confirmed.
      </p>
    </section>

  </article>

  <Footer />
</Base>
